                <h1>academic Department & Course Pathways</h1>
                <h2>1. Department of Computing & Digital Technologies</h2>
                <p>The Department of Computing offers a comprehensive spectrum of undergraduate, postgraduate, and foundation programmes designed to suit applicants with diverse educational backgrounds. Whether you aim to build scalable distributed architectures, secure critical infrastructure against cyber threats, or engineer engaging game engines, our courses combine deep theoretical rigor with industry-standard tooling. </p>
                <ul>
                    <li><b>Core Computing Disciplines: </b>Computer Science, Software Engineering, Cyber Security with Forensics, Computer Networks, and Computer Science for Games.</li>
                    <li><b>Postgraduate Programmes: </b>MSc Computing (conversion pathway for non-computing graduates), MSc Cyber Security, and MPhil Computing and Informatics.</li>
                    <li><b>Foundation Years: </b>Dedicated 4-year programmes providing foundational maths, programming, and web technology principles for students looking to build their entry qualifications.</li>
                </ul>
                <h2>2. Department of Art, Design & Media</h2>
                <p>The Department of Art, Design & Media forms an internationally connected creative community housed under one roof. We encourage interdisciplinary exploration, speculative design, and innovative craftsmanship. Our art and design courses don't just train you in software; they foster alternative ways of thinking, making, communicating, and challenging contemporary culture. </p>
                <ul>
                    <li><b>Core Design Disciplines: </b>Graphic Design, Interior Architecture and Design, Game Design and Development, Digital Media Production, Product Design (BA & BSc routes), and Jewellery, Materials & Design.</li>
                    <li><b>Studio Culture: </b>Students enjoy personal studio spaces, collaborative critique areas, and daily access to specialized digital fabrication and traditional making workshops.</li>    
                </ul>
            </div>

